canvas twice: once after the four corners are painted, and once more after the interior is filled, which is the final grid.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid).copy()\n    H, W = g.shape\n    line = 3\n    rows_div = [y for y in range(H) if np.all(g[y] == line)]\n    cols_div = [x for x in range(W) if np.all(g[:, x] == line)]\n\n    def intervals(divs, n):\n        res, start = [], 0\n        for d in divs + [n]:\n            if d > start:\n                res.append((start, d - 1))\n            start = d + 1\n        return res\n\n    R = intervals(rows_div, H)\n    C = intervals(cols_div, W)\n    nr, nc = len(R), len(C)\n\n    def fill(i, j, col):\n        (y0, y1), (x0, x1) = R[i], C[j]\n        g[y0:y1 + 1, x0:x1 + 1] = col\n\n    fill(0, 0, 2)\n    fill(0, nc - 1, 4)\n    fill(nr - 1, 0, 1)\n    fill(nr - 1, nc - 1, 8)\n    emit(g, \"Paint the four corner cells: top-left 2, top-right 4, bottom-left 1, bottom-right 8.\")\n\n    for i in range(1, nr - 1):\n        for j in range(1, nc - 1):\n            fill(i, j, 7)\n    emit(g, \"Fill every interior cell (not in the first/last cell row or column) with 7.\")\n    return g\n","candidate_tactics":{"panels":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"ines are unevenly spaced, so the cells have different sizes, but they still form a regular table of cell-rows and cell-columns."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Pair 2 has 4 cell-rows and 3 cell-columns, so the middle column's two middle cells are interior."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Pair 3 has 5 cell-columns and 4 cell-rows, so a 3×2 block of cells is interior."}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- **Interior cells** become 7."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Pair 1 has a 3×3 table, so only the centre cell is interior."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Pair 2 has 4 cell-rows and 3 cell-columns, so the middle column's two middle cells are interior."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query